{
  "conformance": "source.admission-merge",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "status": "ruled",
  "basis": [
    "a batch's rows merge by the email account key alone: the first row that is not refused is the prospect, and a later row only fills what the prospect lacks"
  ],
  "rule": "admit(input) over input.rows under input.declaredFields, with input.titleFamilyTable when present. A row keeps only its declared fields; a value is absent when it is missing, empty, white space only, or normalizes to nothing. In input order, a row with no present declared value is refused no_field_survived_allow_list, then one with no email no_identifying_field, then one whose email has no core.email-account-key invalid_email. Rows group only by core.email-account-key: the first row of a group that is not refused is the prospect, and each later row fills only fields the prospect lacks, never replacing a held value, and counts once as duplicate_in_batch. titleFamily is the table's family for the prospect's surviving title. expect.prospects lists each prospect's emailAccountKey and present fields, in contracts/source's names; expect.counts is the batch's counts; no value in expect.appearsNowhere occurs in any output. Values are given already normalized: per-field normalization of the fields compared as deterministic is not specified here and follows in a later version. The merge is within one batch: it names no survivorship mechanism, and matching a prospect to another source's record or to an existing person stays each runtime's own.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "id": "AM-01",
      "input": {
        "declaredFields": [
          "email",
          "title",
          "phone"
        ],
        "rows": [
          {
            "email": "ada@example.com",
            "title": "Head of Events"
          },
          {
            "email": "ada@example.com",
            "phone": "+442079460100"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "prospects": [
          {
            "emailAccountKey": "ada@example.com",
            "title": "Head of Events",
            "phone": "+442079460100"
          }
        ],
        "counts": {
          "in": 2,
          "admitted": 1,
          "rejected": {
            "no_field_survived_allow_list": 0,
            "no_identifying_field": 0,
            "invalid_email": 0,
            "duplicate_in_batch": 1
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "a later row fills a field the prospect lacks: the phone"
    },
    {
      "id": "AM-02",
      "input": {
        "declaredFields": [
          "email",
          "title"
        ],
        "rows": [
          {
            "email": "bo@example.com",
            "title": "Marketing Manager"
          },
          {
            "email": "bo@example.com",
            "title": "Senior Director of Global Marketing"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "prospects": [
          {
            "emailAccountKey": "bo@example.com",
            "title": "Marketing Manager"
          }
        ],
        "counts": {
          "in": 2,
          "admitted": 1,
          "rejected": {
            "no_field_survived_allow_list": 0,
            "no_identifying_field": 0,
            "invalid_email": 0,
            "duplicate_in_batch": 1
          }
        },
        "appearsNowhere": [
          "Senior Director of Global Marketing"
        ]
      },
      "why": "a held value is never replaced, even by a longer one, and the merged-away title appears nowhere"
    },
    {
      "id": "AM-03",
      "input": {
        "declaredFields": [
          "email",
          "title",
          "phone"
        ],
        "rows": [
          {
            "email": "cy@example.com",
            "title": "Head of Events"
          },
          {
            "email": "cy@example.com",
            "phone": "+442079460101"
          },
          {
            "email": "cy@example.com",
            "title": "Marketing Manager",
            "phone": "+442079460102"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "prospects": [
          {
            "emailAccountKey": "cy@example.com",
            "title": "Head of Events",
            "phone": "+442079460101"
          }
        ],
        "counts": {
          "in": 3,
          "admitted": 1,
          "rejected": {
            "no_field_survived_allow_list": 0,
            "no_identifying_field": 0,
            "invalid_email": 0,
            "duplicate_in_batch": 2
          }
        },
        "appearsNowhere": [
          "+442079460102",
          "Marketing Manager"
        ]
      },
      "why": "three rows: the second fills the phone, and the third fills nothing because both fields are held"
    },
    {
